{title: 101 - Children of the Heavenly Father}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: God the Father}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]Children of the heavenly [A]Father Safely [Em]in His [A7]bosom [D]gather;
[D]Nestling [G]bird nor star in [D]heaven Such a [Em]refuge [A7]e'er was gi[D]ven.

Verse 2:
[D]God [A]His [Em]own doth [A7]tend [D]and nourish,
[D]In [G]His [D]holy [Em]love [A7]they [D]flourish;
[D]From [A]all [Em]evil things [A7]He [D]spares them,
[D]In [G]His [D]mighty [Em]arms [A7]He [D]bears them.

Verse 3:
[D]Neither [A]life [Em]nor [A7]death [D]shall ever
[D]From [G]the [D]Lord [Em]His [A7]children [D]sever;
[D]Unto [A]them [Em]His [A7]grace [D]He showeth,
[D]And [G]their [D]sorrows [Em]all [A7]He [D]knoweth.

Verse 4:
[D]Praise [A]the [Em]Lord [A7]in [D]joyful numbers,
[D][G]Your [D]Protector [Em][A7]never [D]slumbers;
[D]At [A]the [Em]will [A7]of [D]your Defender
[D][G]Every [D]foe-man [Em][A7]must [D]surrender.

Verse 5:
[D]Though [A]He [Em]giveth [A7]or [D]He taketh,
[D][G]God [D]His [Em]children [A7]ne'er [D]forsaketh;
[D]His [A]the [Em]loving [A7]purpose [D]solely
[D]To [G]preserve [D]them [Em]pure [A7]and [D]holy.
